<title>BELGIUM: French, German EMU forecasts &quot;on safe side&quot;-source.</title>
<headline>French, German EMU forecasts &quot;on safe side&quot;-source.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>All current indications suggest that French and German forecasts on economic convergence ahead of monetary union are &quot;on the safe side&quot;, an EU source said on Monday.</p>
<p>Earlier European Union finance ministers reviewed convergence programmes submitted by France and Germany in which France forecasts a deficit to GDP ratio this year of 3.0 percent and Germany forecasts a ratio of 2.9 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;All the indications for the moment allow us to believe that their forecasts are on the safe side,&quot; the source said. -- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
